$string['categorycovervideomaxbytes_desc'] = 'How large the cover video of a category may be. The upload limit of the site still applies on top of this one, so the field is bounded by whichever of the two is smaller. Twenty megabytes is a few seconds of 720p, which is what a card preview is.';
$string['categoryfilterfields'] = 'Filter groups';
$string['categoryfilterfields_desc'] = 'Up to four course custom fields of the dropdown menu type, each becoming a group of filter pills on the category page with the number of courses behind every option. A field appears here once it exists in the course custom fields of the site; the landing page fields "Enrolment page model" and "Modality" are two candidates.';
$string['categoryfilterfields_toomany'] = 'Choose at most {$a} fields.';
$string['categoryhero_appearance'] = 'Appearance';
$string['categoryhero_badge1'] = 'Badge 1';
$string['categoryhero_badge1_help'] = 'The institutional badge of the category, shown on the category page and on the category\'s card in the course index. PNG or SVG with a transparent background, fitted inside its box and never cropped. The file name without its extension is the alternative text of the image, with hyphens and underscores read as spaces: name the file after the institution. Up to three badges are shown, in the order of these three fields; an empty one is skipped and the row closes the gap. One file per field: adding another replaces the one that is there, and deleting it removes the badge from every page.';
$string['categoryhero_badge2'] = 'Badge 2';
$string['categoryhero_badge2_help'] = 'The second badge of the category. Same rules as the first one: one file, replaced by adding another and removed by deleting it.';
$string['categoryhero_badge3'] = 'Badge 3';
$string['categoryhero_badge3_help'] = 'The third badge of the category. Same rules as the first one: one file, replaced by adding another and removed by deleting it.';
$string['categoryhero_bgcolour'] = 'Background colour';
$string['categoryhero_bgcolour_help'] = 'The colour of the band behind the category\'s name, written as #rrggbb. Any colour: the swatch beside the field opens your browser\'s colour picker, and the panel below measures the pair while you type. A pair reading under 4.5:1 is refused when you save - the WCAG AA minimum for normal text, which the tagline and the public page text on the band are.';
$string['categoryhero_cardsummary'] = 'Card text';
$string['categoryhero_cardsummary_help'] = 'The text under the category\'s name on its card, in its parent category\'s page and in the course index. Plain text, at most 160 characters, which is where the card cuts a description. Leave it empty and the card shows the beginning of the category description instead. The category\'s own page keeps showing the description in its header either way.';
