$string['loginpage_custom'] = 'Custom login page';
$string['loginpage_desc'] = 'The theme\'s login page: the institutional panel of the registration page beside the two ways in, each named after the people it serves - the organisation\'s Google account first, then the username and password form, nothing hidden behind a tab. While it is shown, the login page settings of Boost Union (arrangement, layout, order, instructions, branding, buttons) do not apply; info banners and the footnote still do. The panel shows Boost Union\'s compact logo; without one, the band logo uploaded in the access screens settings of auth_loginsteps when that plugin is installed, and the site\'s short name otherwise. An identity provider\'s mark is drawn locally, so no image is ever fetched from the provider\'s servers. Every text on the page is a language string, editable through Language customisation. \'Leave it to Boost Union\' restores its login page exactly as configured there.';
$string['loginpageheading'] = 'The login page';
$string['loginpanelfoot'] = 'Monitoring notice';
